    <item>
      <title>Odoo on Ubuntu: How I Installed It</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/odoo/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 11 Aug 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/odoo/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-i-did&#34;&gt;What I Did&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I installed &lt;strong&gt;Odoo&lt;/strong&gt; (open-source ERP) on Ubuntu for a project. These are the exact steps I ran — all &lt;code&gt;apt&lt;/code&gt; commands on Ubuntu.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo apt update &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; sudo apt upgrade
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;create-an-odoo-user&#34;&gt;Create an Odoo User&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run this command to create a system user for Odoo:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo adduser -system -home&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;/opt/odoo -group odoo
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;install-postgresql&#34;&gt;Install PostgreSQL&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Odoo needs PostgreSQL as its database, so install it with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo apt-get install postgresql -y
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;create-a-postgresql-user-for-odoo&#34;&gt;Create a PostgreSQL User for Odoo&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo su - postgres -c &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;createuser -s odoo&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; 2&amp;gt; /dev/null &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; true
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;install-python-dependencies&#34;&gt;Install Python Dependencies&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Odoo requires some Python packages. Install them with:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
